{{en-noun}}

# Something which can be appended to something else.
# {{context|computer hardware|software|lang=en}} A [[software]] extension or [[hardware]] [[peripheral]] that provides additional functions or customization for a core application or system.
#* '''2010''', Kenneth Baldauf, Ralph Stair, ''Succeeding with Technology'' (page 77)
#*: Microdrives that can hold several gigabytes (see Figure 2.20) have been available as '''add-ons''' for portable devices.
# {{context|poker|lang=en}} Additional [[chip]]s that can be [[purchase]]d at specific times in tournament play.

